A"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-7280466-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7280466</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-8094280-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>8094280</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9089484-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9089484</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1085286A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EBARA CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE NAOYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUBARA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EBARA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, NAOYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUBARA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE NAOYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUBARA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, NAOYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUBARA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A plate type heat exchanger capable of exchanging heat by laminating plates and passing two types of fluids between the plates alternately, wherein a heat exchange element (2) is formed of a set of two plates (3) having recessed and projected parts and an opening part (5) at both ends in longitudinal direction which are overlapped with each other at their peripheral edges, a plurality of heat exchange elements (2) are formed by overlapping the opening parts (5) with each other, a space (11) between two sheets of plates (3) forming the heat exchange elements (2) is used as a first fluid path, a space (12) between the heat exchange elements (2) is used as a path for another fluid which is in the heat exchange relation with the first fluid, whereby the plates (3) are used as the heat transfer surface for both fluids, and the second fluid path which is in contact with that element at its peripheral edge part (4) and sealed is formed when the heat exchange elements (2) are overlapped with each other.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un échangeur thermique du type à plaques capable d'échanger la chaleur en laminant des plaques et en passant en alternance deux types de fluides entre ces plaques. Un élément d'échange thermique (2) est constitué d'un jeu de deux plaques (3) présentant des parties évidées et saillantes et une partie d'ouverture (5) au niveau des deux extrémités dans le sens longitudinal, lesquelles parties sont superposées l'une à l'autre au niveau de leur pourtour. Une pluralité d'éléments d'échange thermique (2) sont constitués par la superposition des parties d'ouverture. Un espace (11) situé entre les éléments d'échange thermique (2) est utilisé comme voie pour un autre fluide qui se trouve en relation d'échange thermique avec le premier fluide. Les plaques (3) servent de surface de transfert thermique pour les deux fluides tandis que la seconde voie fluidique, qui se trouve en contact avec cet élément au niveau de son pourtour (4) est qui est scellée, se forme lorsque les éléments d'échange thermique (2) sont superposés.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>